<!-- Display configuration of the built-in panel of the Lenovo Yoga Tab Plus.

     The backlight scale (0 to 1) is the one of Android, with the high brightness
     mode of the panel on top: up to 0.85 the normal range of the panel (the
     brightness curve of the previous configuration, 650 nits at the end), above
     it the range with the "hbm" node of the panel on, up to 900 nits (the typical
     and the peak brightness of the specifications of the panel). LenovoHbmBridge
     sends it as the "hbm" node and a backlight value of the composer.

     The HDR brightness has the shape of the Pixel configuration (cheetah): the HDR
     peak is the maximum of the normal range for most of the screen brightnesses, and
     the high brightness mode is only used when the screen brightness is high. -->
